            <div xml:id="d525">

                <pb facs="0979" n="855" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg855"/>

                <head>No. 521.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Evarts to Mr.
                    Christiancy.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-11-27"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 27,
                        1880</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 109.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I subjoin the text of a telegram which was
                    sent to Mr. Osborn, envoy extraordinary and minister plenipotentiary of the
                    United States at Santiago, by this Department on the 19th instant: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>You are authorized to unite with your colleagues in pressing upon Chili
                            the adoption of the measures agreed upon in a diplomatic conference at
                            Lima for securing the lives and property of neutrals when Lima is
                            attacked. This authority is to be used only in case these measures are
                            approved by Christiancy and yourself as within neutral policy and this
                            concurrent representation seems to you useful. You are also authorized
                            to join in asking a direct answer from Chili, if in your judgment the
                            requirement is justified by the situation. Telegraph your action.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>I am, sir, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. M. EVARTS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
